course: dictionary
lesson: 9263
title: Southern: which part, which way
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Southern is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you which part of a place something is in, or which way something faces. «Local words belong to real dialects: in the southern US "y'all" means you all.» Here southern tells you which part of the US the words come from.
explain: Southern can also mean facing or going towards the south. Picture a map with north at the top. Southern is the bottom part. «The real king is in trouble: wild lions have lost most of the land they once roamed across Africa, southern Europe and Asia.» Southern Europe is the south part of Europe.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in "the south part of" and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have got it. «Southern Europe» becomes «the south part of Europe», so it works.
fact: Southern means in or from the south part of a place, or facing or going towards the south.
fact: The Southern Hemisphere is the half of the Earth south of the equator. It includes Australia, New Zealand, South Africa and most of South America.
fact: In the Southern Hemisphere the seasons are the opposite of the north, so Christmas comes in summer.
fact: The Southern Ocean surrounds Antarctica.
fact: The Southern Cross, Crux, is the smallest of the 88 constellations.
exercise: What does Southern Hemisphere mean? | The part of the sea near the top of the map | The middle of the Earth | The half of the Earth north of the equator | *The half of the Earth south of the equator
exercise: Mia lives in the southern part of England. Where does she live? | *In the south of England | In the north of England | In the middle of the sea | In Antarctica
exercise: Which of these is a place in the Southern Hemisphere? | Canada | Norway | *New Zealand | Iceland
test: Christmas comes in summer in New Zealand. Why? | *Because the seasons in the Southern Hemisphere are the opposite of the north | Because the Southern Cross is bright in December | Because the sun is closer to New Zealand in December | Because Christmas always falls on the hottest day
test: Which group of stars is the smallest of the 88 constellations? | Big Dipper | Plough | Orion | *Southern Cross
exam: Which phrase means the same as southern part? | the top of the map | the middle of the land | *the south part | the north side
